## How Search Works in Slough

Slough's position between the M4 and Heathrow shapes who searches for Slough businesses.

The town is served by junctions 5, 6 and 7 of the M4, sits about 5 miles from Heathrow Airport, and has Elizabeth line services from its stations at Slough, Langley and Burnham ([Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slough)).

Most Slough firms deal with three kinds of searcher.

**Residents** looking for trades, clinics, solicitors, accountants and shops near home. These searches run through Google's map results, so your Google Business Profile, your reviews and a service page that names Slough and your part of it do most of the work.

**Businesses buying from businesses.** Procurement teams, facilities managers and engineers search for a capability, a standard or a supplier near their site. They judge you on detailed service pages and evidence, not on a map listing.

**People passing through.** Heathrow, the M4 and the rail links bring in travellers, contractors and staff from outside the borough. Hotels, food, parking, car services and venues need to show up in the searches people make before they arrive and on the day.

## Slough in Numbers

Slough is a borough of small businesses: nine in ten have fewer than 10 staff.

| Slough borough | Figure | Source |
|---|---:|---|
| VAT or PAYE registered businesses, 2026 | 6,780 | ONS UK Business Counts |
| Share with fewer than 10 staff | 90.2% | ONS UK Business Counts |
| Population, 2021 Census | 158,500 | ONS Census 2021 |
| Population change, 2011 to 2021 | +13.0% | ONS Census 2021 |
| Data centres on Slough Trading Estate, July 2025 | 31 | SEGRO |

Slough had 6,780 VAT or PAYE registered businesses in 2026, and 90.2% of them employ fewer than 10 people ([ONS UK Business Counts, enterprises by local authority, March 2026](https://www.nomisweb.co.uk/datasets/idbrent), released with [UK business: activity, size and location 2026](https://www.ons.gov.uk/businessindustryandtrade/business/activitysizeandlocation/bulletins/ukbusinessactivitysizeandlocation/2026)). Its population grew 13.0% between 2011 and 2021, to 158,500 ([ONS](https://www.ons.gov.uk/visualisations/censuspopulationchange/E06000039/)).

So most Slough businesses are small: a few people, one website and no in-house marketer. That is why I start with a fixed-fee audit rather than a monthly commitment.

## Slough Trading Estate and B2B Firms

Slough Trading Estate is the main reason so many Slough firms sell to other businesses rather than to the public.

SEGRO describes Slough Trading Estate as a 420-acre site it has owned since it was established in 1920, and the largest industrial estate in single ownership in Europe. In a letter to Slough Borough Council dated 11 July 2025, SEGRO said there were 31 data centres on the estate, with one more under construction ([Slough Borough Council](https://www.slough.gov.uk/downloads/file/4911/appendix-i-1-data-centre-development-segro)).

For firms based there, or supplying the businesses that are, the map results are rarely the main problem. Their buyers search for a capability or a product, often from anywhere in the UK. A single "Services" page does not win those searches.

What usually works better:

- One page per capability, with the specifications, sectors and standards a buyer checks
- Case studies and certifications on the page, where a buyer and Google can both see them
- A site structure that makes the link between your services clear
- Content that answers the questions buyers ask before they shortlist a supplier

I'll help you decide which searches are worth owning and build the pages that can earn them, through [topical authority](/services/topical-authority/) and [content architecture](/services/topical-maps/) work.

## What I Do for Slough Businesses

I offer four kinds of work to Slough businesses, and most clients start with the audit.

**[Local SEO](/services/local-seo/)**: Google Business Profile categories and services, a steady flow of reviews, consistent name, address and phone details across directories, and pages written for Slough searches rather than for "Berkshire" in general.

**[Technical SEO audit](/services/technical-seo-audit/)**: a fixed £495 check of crawling, indexing, page speed, mobile layout, structured data and site structure, with a ranked list of fixes you or your developer can act on.

**[Semantic SEO](/services/semantic-seo/) and content**: for B2B and technology firms whose buyers research before they get in touch, I map the questions those buyers ask and build pages that answer them properly.

**[AI search visibility](/services/ai-search-optimisation/)**: I check whether ChatGPT, Google AI Overviews and similar tools mention your business when people ask about your service in Slough, then fix the gaps in what they can find about you.

